hello everyone and welcome to my first  ever jake's take where i talk about the  good the bad and the ugly of a newly  released game and let you know if you  should buy it or not i recently played  dimija on stream so i thought it'd be a  good game to start this series on  especially since it's been considered a  souls like from software game that's  been drawing comparisons to bloodborne  and sakiro and are people right in  comparing thiamisia to those two games  that i really consider masterpieces in  terms of thimesia's combat system it's  pretty much like mixing those two games  together and to put it bluntly it's  awesome diameter's combat system is fun  to learn plain and simple you have a  standard saber attack and a claw attack  that are meant to affect two different  health bars that every enemy in the game  has the normal health bar and the green  health bar staber attacks damage the  white bar claw attacks damage the green  bar pretty simple to understand very  difficult to master each enemy has a  different moveset that you'll have to  learn or this game will absolutely  destroy you it's not an easy game in the  beginning but you get used to the combat  very easily you can dodge attacks that  remind me of the dodging sidestep  mechanics of bloodborne or you can use  the more effective deflect mechanic that  reminds me a lot of sakiro that keeps  you playing aggressively which this game  highly favors if you were a fan of  sakura's skill tree then you'll be a  major fan of themes leveling and talent  trees leveling is very simple you can  increase your damage health or plague  status each level you put in will also  give you talent points to spend with all  kinds of different abilities these  include saber deflect dodge claw  feathers and strategies all of which  have different sub talents for you to  invest points into the cool part is you  can move these talents around whenever  you want to create different character  builds on the fly without having to  stress too much on the talents that you  pick in the moment when you hold down  the claw ability you can steal away claw  attacks from enemies to use against them  you can also find or learn your own  special claw attacks that you can equip  to your character to have every time you  deflect an enemy you've also got your  potions that are just your general  healing abilities there's three  different kinds of healing to choose  from short long and fast healing i  really never felt it necessary to change  from the base healing potions and just  upgraded that to make it better but  having the options for players to  customize even their healing abilities  is pretty cool to put it short the  combat system is fun to learn it runs  deep with customization and it's very  addictive to try and master the flow of  combat is the true meat of this game  which is why i'm not worried about  showing you guys any spoilers the  experience is in the gameplay even with  the sometimes janky mechanics that can  get stuck in walls from time to time i  still had a ton of fun playing this game  the boss fights are creative  entertaining and learning their move  sets reminds me of any souls game i've  ever played the one gimmick boss i came  across was the worst boss i've ever  experienced in any game ever even worse  than the bet of chaos in my opinion but  once you get through it you never have  to do it again however the main bosses  and even most of the side bosses are  amazing my fight against old took me  over an hour to beat and i loved every  second of it the payoff was totally  worth it and gave me flashbacks of the  first time i ever played any souls game  and the best part of it is this boss is  completely optional that boss was so  cool so well designed so pretty with  beautiful animations with beautiful  soundtrack in the back that's a s tier  boss  so cool so much fun to learn great  payoff after doing it freaking sick  however where thinesha falls short is  just the overall story there's no voice  acting and a ton of reading and most of  it is pretty basic posters or notes that  give you a bit of lore about the area  maybe an upcoming boss and sometimes the  overall point of the game you can also  beat this game in less than four hours  if you just fly through all the main  areas i'd say there's an additional  eight hours of optional content for you  to play which includes one of the best  boss fights i've ever played and also  one of the worst so the optional stuff  can be pretty hit or miss especially  since the other optional areas are just  destroying or finding certain items now  there is definitely a story here and the  atmosphere of each level is pretty cool  but i didn't really care enough to learn  it at least for me the story here i  didn't take much interest in but when i  learned this game was made by a  development team of less than 10 people  i really just let everything slide and  played the game for what it was so was  it worth the 20 i paid for the game  absolutely are you going to get more  than one playthrough out of this game  you could there's some replayability in  the way you can build your character but  other than that you likely will only  play through this game once i can  definitely see players speed running  this game trying to beat all the bosses  as fast as possible that could be really  cool nymeja is a good game with an  amazing combat system that you should  play if you have the means to do so for  myself i was really surprised how much i  enjoyed it once i got deeper into the  game i was addicted to the flow of  combat in less than an hour and i felt  like the price of admission was worth  every penny thank you all for watching  let me know if you'd like to see more  jake's takes videos like this do all the  nice youtube stuff to help you grow the  channel if you want to and i will see  you all in the next video take care
 

